        "en" to GemDetails(
            "The spider conch (Lambis lambis) is a herbivorous gastropod of Indo-Pacific coral reefs and shallow seagrass beds. It moves in little hops using its muscular foot, which ends in a sickle-shaped operculum, and grazes on fine algae. In adults, the mantle forms a thick lip extended by six long hollow digitations that give the shell its spider outline; these spines stabilise the shell on the bottom and protect it from predators. Like other conchs, it watches its surroundings with stalked eyes that emerge through notches in the shell.",
